!! tools/seat-broker.mjs  (data-only git plumbing; NEVER executes lane code, never checks out with filters, never touches submodules/hooks/installs)
Pinned absolute binaries: GIT = "/usr/bin/git" (existence checked; no PATH lookup anywhere).
* `export function brokerEnv(iso)` -> EXACT object with only: PATH "/usr/bin:/bin" is NOT allowed to hold lane or home dirs, use "/usr/bin:/bin"; HOME `${iso}/home`; TMPDIR `${iso}/tmp`; XDG_CONFIG_HOME `${iso}/home`; LC_ALL "C"; GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM "1"; GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL "/dev/null"; GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT "0"; GIT_ATTR_NOSYSTEM "1"; GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS "0". Nothing inherited from process.env. (The test allows only those keys.)
* Internal `git(ctx, args, {input, env, cwd})` = spawnSync(GIT, ["-c","core.hooksPath=/dev/null","-c","core.fsmonitor=false","-c","core.attributesFile=/dev/null","-c","credential.helper=","-c","core.sshCommand=/usr/bin/ssh","&#45;-git-dir",ctx.gitDir, ...args], {env: brokerEnv(ctx.iso) plus extras, input}) ; mkdir iso/home and iso/tmp first. Output capped to 8192 chars in `output`.
* `export async function readSafe(worktree, rel)` -> `{mode: "100644"|"100755", content: Buffer}`. Refuse (reject Error with the words used in tests): absolute or ".." rel ("invalid path"); any lstat on a path component being a symlink ("symlink"); a directory or non-regular file ("not a regular file"); a gitlink/submodule path (a directory containing .git or listed as mode 160000 in HEAD: "gitlink"). Race-proof: open the final file with fs.open(path, O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW), then readlink(`/proc/self/fd/${fd}`) and require it to equal realpath(worktree)+"/"+rel (else "outside"), fstat must be a regular file, read the bytes from the fd. Never read by path after the check.
* `export async function commitWithReceipt(ctx, {paths, messageFile, expectHead})` -> `{ok, output, head?, tree?}`. ctx = {gitDir, worktree, iso, branch, author:{name,email}, receiptsDir, keyFile, requiredChecks:[names], checks:[{name,argv}], bwrap:boolean}. Steps: head = `rev-parse refs/heads/${branch}`; if expectHead !== head refuse with output containing "expected old head"; paths nonempty; for each path readSafe (a path deleted from the worktree but tracked in HEAD becomes a removal). Build a TEMP index in iso/tmp (GIT_INDEX_FILE env extra): `read-tree HEAD`, for each file `hash-object -w --no-filters --stdin` (content on stdin, NO path argument so no attribute/filter applies) then `update-index --add --cacheinfo <mode>,<sha>,<path>`; removals `update-index --force-remove -- path`; refuse a path whose HEAD entry mode is 160000 ("gitlink"). `write-tree` -> tree. Receipt: verifyReceipt({keyFile, receiptsDir, tree, requiredChecks}); if absent, run `runCheckSeat({...ctx, tree})` (from ./seat-walls.mjs) which writes the signed receipt; if the seat fails refuse with output naming "check" and the failing check; verify again. Message: read messageFile bytes (must be a regular file, no symlink). `commit-tree <tree> -p <head> -F` via stdin message with env GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and GIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL set from ctx.author and a fixed date left to git. `update-ref refs/heads/${branch} <new> <head>` (compare-and-swap on the old head). Then bring the REAL index to match for the committed paths with the same update-index &#45;-cacheinfo / &#45;-force-remove calls on the real index (GIT_INDEX_FILE unset, default `${gitDir}/index`). No hooks fire, no porcelain commit/add/checkout.
* `export async function pushWithGo(ctx & {goFile})` -> `{ok, output}`. goFile must have exactly two lines: branch then head sha. Read it, then DELETE it (the go spends on the attempt, before any check result is returned, even when it refuses; if the file is absent: output "no push-go from the controller"). Refuse (output contains "go") if branch !== ctx.branch, or head !== current `refs/heads/${branch}` sha, or the file lacks two lines. Push: `git push origin ${head}:refs/heads/${branch}` with the pinned GIT and the fixed `-c` set above, env = brokerEnv plus HOME = the REAL home (os.userInfo().homedir) only for this call so the controller's ssh keys work; never -u, never &#45;-force.
* `export async function addWorktree(ctx, {path, branch, base})` -> `{ok, output}`. `worktree add --no-checkout -b ${branch} ${path} ${base}` then fill the tree with NO filters and NO submodules: export base with `archive --format=tar ${base}` piped to `/usr/bin/tar -x -C ${path}` (pinned tar; ignore export-subst irrelevance), then in the new worktree set its index to base with `read-tree ${base}` using GIT_INDEX_FILE=\&lt;that worktree's index path from `rev-parse --git-path index` run with &#45;-git-dir of the new worktree> . Gitlink paths stay empty directories (mkdir if archive omitted them). Write NO submodule config. The destination must not exist yet.
* `export function verifyReceipt({keyFile, receiptsDir, tree, requiredChecks})` -> `{ok, reason?}`: reads `${receiptsDir}/${tree}.json` `{tree, checks, mac}`; recompute `signReceipt({keyFile, tree, checks})` mac with timingSafeEqual; require receipt.tree === tree and every requiredChecks name present in receipt.checks.

