!! tools/seat-walls.mjs  (the CHECK SEAT and INSTALL SEAT: the only places lane code runs, always behind bubblewrap)
* `export const HAVE_BWRAP` = existsSync("/usr/bin/bwrap") && a spawnSync("/usr/bin/bwrap",["&#45;-ro-bind","/","/","/usr/bin/true"]) that exits 0.
* `export function signReceipt({keyFile, tree, checks})` -> `{tree, checks, mac}` with mac = HMAC-SHA256(hex) keyed by the key file's bytes over `${tree}\n${checks.slice().sort().join(",")}`.
* `export async function runCheckSeat({gitDir, tree, checks, keyFile, receiptsDir, iso, bwrap, keepWork})` -> `{ok, output, work?}`. TRUSTED parent process: makes a fresh work dir under iso/tmp, exports the exact tree: `/usr/bin/git --git-dir gitDir archive --format=tar ${tree}` into `${work}/tree` (pinned tar). For each check {name, argv}: run argv under `/usr/bin/bwrap --die-with-parent --new-session --unshare-pid --unshare-ipc --unshare-net --clearenv --ro-bind / / --tmpfs /tmp --tmpfs <real home> --dev /dev --proc /proc --bind ${work}/tree /work/tree... ` Concretely: bind the work dir read-write at /work (so the seat writes only /work, and tests read `${work}/out`), `--chdir /work/tree`, env set with &#45;-setenv to only PATH=/usr/bin:/bin HOME=/work/home LC_ALL=C. Everything else read-only (so a ref or go-file write fails), /tmp and the real home hidden by tmpfs, no network. A non-zero exit fails the seat: `{ok:false, output: "check <name> failed: ..."}` and NO receipt is written. If bwrap is false, refuse with output "no wall available" (never run unwalled). On all-pass write `signReceipt(...)` JSON to `${receiptsDir}/${tree}.json` (mkdir receiptsDir) and return ok. Remove the work dir unless keepWork (then return `work`). Only the PARENT ever reads keyFile; the sandboxed child never sees it (it sits under /tmp hidden by tmpfs or is otherwise unreadable: tests put it under os.tmpdir()).
* `export async function runInstallSeat({worktree, gitDir, pnpm, storeDir, iso, protect, env})` -> `{ok, output}`. First read `${worktree}/.npmrc` if present: allow ONLY keys registry, store-dir, strict-peer-dependencies, auto-install-peers, shamefully-hoist, node-linker, public-hoist-pattern; any other key refuses with output naming that key (keys may look like `//registry.evil/:_authToken`). Then run `pnpm install --offline --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts --store-dir ${storeDir}` (the pinned pnpm path given) with cwd = worktree under bwrap: &#45;-ro-bind / /, then &#45;-bind worktree worktree (rw), &#45;-bind storeDir storeDir (rw), &#45;-ro-bind gitDir gitDir (so .git is read-only even though it sits inside the worktree), each `protect` path ro, &#45;-tmpfs /tmp, &#45;-tmpfs real home, &#45;-unshare-net &#45;-unshare-pid &#45;-die-with-parent &#45;-clearenv with only PATH=/usr/bin:/bin:\&lt;dir of pnpm>, HOME=${iso}/home... NOTE the test fake pnpm logs `env` lines matching ^(NODE_OPTIONS|npm_config_|GIT_|HOME)= and expects NODE_OPTIONS, npm_config_*, GIT_* absent (HOME may appear); `env` option passed by the caller is IGNORED for the child (it exists to prove poison is dropped). The fake writes its log to a path outside the worktree under os.tmpdir(): that path is hidden by &#45;-tmpfs /tmp, so bind-mount the log's DIRECTORY? NO: instead do not tmpfs /tmp; bind /tmp read-only (it is part of &#45;-ro-bind /) and keep the test's log writable by additionally accepting an optional `extraRw` array of paths to bind read-write (add `extraRw: [logDir]` support; the lead will pass it). If bwrap is false refuse with "no wall available".
Hand back by final message: files created, anything unclear.

NOTE for runInstallSeat mount order: bind extraRw read-write first, then the gitDir read-only, then each `protect` path read-only LAST (later mounts win), so the test's controller dir stays unwritable although its parent is bound rw. The test passes extraRw: [x.root] and protect: [x.control].

